 "co_sharkstooth_northeast_ridge": {
  "area": "co_sharkstooth",
  "set": {
   "approach": "Start from the Glacier Gorge trailhead and follow the trail past Loch Vale. Just beyond the lake, turn right onto the Andrew's Glacier trail; the split comes right after a creek crossing and is easy to miss. Follow that trail to just short of the Andrew's campground sign, where a faint path turns hard left and uphill into The Gash, a large boulder field. Sharkstooth appears on the left; work up through the boulders, staying low near the glacial runoff, to the base of the ridge. Raptor closures can apply to this part of the park in spring and early summer, so check current park closures.",
   "descent_text": "From the summit, head southeast down a gully to the first rappel anchors, following cairns. Bolted stations lead down in three rappels, after which a class 3 downclimb reaches the top of The Gash, and you return by the approach. The descent is the same line used by the East Gully route. Rockfall is the main hazard, so call out when pulling ropes, and check each anchor before trusting it, since some old pins and webbing remain."
  },
  "review": {
   "sources": [
    "https://www.mountainproject.com/area/105745133/sharkstooth?print=1",
    "https://www.mountainproject.com/route/105750940/northeast-ridge?print=1",
    "https://mountainproject.com/route/105750994/east-gully?print=1"
   ],
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Area page and route page agree on the three rappels, the gully to the first anchor and the class 3 downclimb into The Gash; rope length left out because sources differ. Approach from the area page, matched by the route page."
  }
